{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>I would bear its loss.</b> If it was torn [prey], the offense was upon me, and I would repay its like." "I was stolen by day. The yod is added like the yod of מלאתי (Isaiah 1:21), and so it is: whether stolen by day or by night, you would demand it of my hand."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:38.073127493Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}